<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's March net foreign debt down at $12.57bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary's March net foreign debt down at $12.57bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net foreign debt dropped to $12,570.3 million in March from $12,754.2 million in February, the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Tuesday in a statement.</p>
<p>    FIGURES IN $MILLION	    March 1997   Feb 1997</p>
<p> Net foreign debt of Hungary    12,570.3	12,754.2</p>
<p>International reserves and</p>
<p>   other foreign assets	   12,347.3	12,155.4</p>
<p> International reserves	    8,510.9	 8,639.3</p>
<p>    - Gold				  35.1	    36.4</p>
<p> Gross foreign debt		 24,442.5	24,440.8</p>
<p>Net foreign debt of the</p>
<p>   government and the NBH	  7,570.1	 7,354.4</p>
<p>Gross foreign debt of the</p>
<p>   government and the NBH	 16,852.9	16,777.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Debt figures exclude inter-company loans. The NBH values gold at London market prices.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1)0327 4040</p>
</text>
